meta {
  name: Get Subscription Entitlements
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/subscription/entitlements
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: DPoP {{oauthAccessToken}}
  DPoP: {{dpopProof}}
}

docs {
  Returns {viewerDid, plan: "free" | "pro"} for the verified OAuth viewer. Response is private, no-store. Until billing is integrated, configure SOCIALWIRE_PRO_DIDS on Gateway as comma-separated exact DIDs; an unset allowlist grants nobody Pro. Pro enforcement defaults off. Enable SOCIALWIRE_PRO_GATING_ENABLED on Gateway together with NEXT_PUBLIC_PRO_GATING_ENABLED on Web (requires a Web rebuild). Plans still reflect grants when enforcement is disabled. With enforcement enabled, a linked brand authenticates as its own DID and requires an explicit grant for creator analytics; an owner's grant is not inherited. Request parameters, plan headers, and local client storage cannot grant entitlements. Analytics summary/refresh return 403 ProRequired for Free viewers only with enforcement enabled; ordinary Reader/Social analytics observations remain available.
}
